# Master Page Generator — Learnings Log

## 2026-06-13 - SpngTargetMap (Spinning Standards/Targets) Master Page
- **MuiForm API changes detected:** N/A — the jute-production masters do NOT use MuiForm/IndexWrapper. They use the simpler single-file pattern: raw MUI DataGrid + MUI Dialog + plain TextField/MenuItem state. Reference: drawingMachineAttr/page.tsx, trollyMaster/page.tsx. The agent spec's "MuiForm dialog" template did NOT apply here; the local convention is the authority.
- **Pattern drift from spec:** Significant. dashboardportal/juteProduction/masters/* do not import IndexWrapper or @/components/ui/muiform at all. Correct pattern observed:
  - useSelectedCompanyCoId() -> { coId } (string) from localStorage; NOT from a "co_id" prop.
  - useSidebarContext() -> { selectedCompany, selectedBranches }; branch options = selectedCompany.branches filtered by selectedBranches; single-branch auto-selected.
  - fetchWithCookie<T>(url, method, body) from @/utils/apiClient2 returns { data, error, status }; responses are double-wrapped: data.data holds the payload ({"data": ...}).
  - api consts imported from @/utils/api as `apiRoutesPortalMasters` (NOT the spec's fetchWithCookie+apiClient2-only mention).
  - EDIT/DELETE consts are base path strings; caller appends `/${id}` (and `?co_id=` query where the backend needs it). CREATE puts co_id in the body.
- **Dependent dropdown issues:** id_type (mcid/qid) -> ref_id cascade. Solved by deriving ref options from the single SETUP payload (machines vs qualities) via a memoized refOptionsFor(idType) helper, and resetting ref_id to "" whenever id_type changes (in both the filter bar and the create dialog). No extra fetch needed — setup returns both lists up front.
- **What worked well:** Single SETUP fetch on mount for all dialog options + a separate LIST fetch (re-run on filter change via useMemo'd filters in the refresh callback dep array). Mirroring trollyMaster's branch handling verbatim avoided hydration/branch bugs.
- **What should change:** The agent spec is written around dashboardportal/masters/ (categoryMaster/itemMaster, MuiForm+IndexWrapper). For dashboardportal/juteProduction/masters/ the live convention is the lighter single-file DataGrid+Dialog pattern. Spec should note this divergence per-area and tell future runs to ALWAYS read a sibling in the SAME masters subtree first.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** juteProduction masters use single-file page.tsx (no _components/hooks/types split, no MuiForm, no IndexWrapper). Edit endpoint for this entity only accepts {effective_date, value, active} — id_type/ref_id/value_role/param are immutable after create, so the dialog disables those fields in edit mode.
- **Verification:** `npx tsc --noEmit` shows ZERO errors in the new file; the only 3 project errors are pre-existing in jutePurchase/mr/components/MRPreview.test.tsx (unrelated).

## 2026-06-13 - Spinning SQC (juteSQC/spinning) — two-tab daily-entry screen (NOT a classic master)
- **MuiForm API changes detected:** N/A — this build deliberately did NOT use the IndexWrapper+MuiForm dialog master pattern. The task said "mirror spreader's tab pattern", so the canonical reference was `juteProduction/spreader/` (page.tsx + _components + hooks + types + utils), a daily-entry/transaction-style screen, not a CRUD master.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** New (4th) frontend pattern, confirms the prior entry's drift note from the other angle: "Daily-entry tab page" = page.tsx (mounted-gate + branch resolution + date pickers + Tabs) -> _components/<Form>.tsx + <Grid>.tsx -> hooks/use*.ts (one hook = one endpoint, version-counter `refresh()`, `cancelled` abort flag, `{data}` unwrap via fetchWithCookie) -> types/*Types.ts. Forms POST then call onSaved(); grids are read-only or delete-only. Dominant across spreader/ and spinning/. The spec's Architecture Decision table has no row for this.
- **Two patterns coexist in juteSQC/:** the MuiForm+IndexWrapper+Dialog master pattern (juteSQC/r-08-01 Morrah-Weight) AND the spreader-style tab page (this build). The deciding factor is the sibling page the task points at, NOT the directory.
- **Branch resolution block is now standard (same as prior entry):** sidebarBranchIds = selectedBranches.map(Number); 1 auto-selects, >1 shows a Branch <TextField select>, 0 shows a warning Alert. Copied verbatim from spreader/page.tsx.
- **Data-fetch helper (matches prior entry):** fetchWithCookie<T> -> { data, error, status }; responses double-wrapped (resp.data.data). coId is a STRING; pass as-is in query string, Number(coId) in POST bodies. *_DELETE consts are base paths; caller appends `/${id}?co_id=${coId}`.
- **Multi-observation vs upsert:** Tab 2 count readings are append-only (each Add Reading = one new row, NOT upsert); Tab 1 speed/TPI is one active row per mc+quality+date. Modeled the count grid getRowId with a fallback composite key since the backend PK field name was unconfirmed (tolerated jute_sqc_spinning_count_id / sqc_spinning_count_id / id).
- **Dependent dropdown issues:** none in these two tabs.
- **What worked well:** Inlined a local todayISO() in page.tsx instead of importing spreader/utils/shift.ts, keeping the new screen self-contained under juteSQC/ and honoring "do NOT edit other modules' dirs".
- **What should change:** (1) Add the daily-entry-tab-page row to the Architecture Decision table, reference spreader/. (2) Broaden the Self-Improvement "scan recent master pages" git glob beyond dashboardportal/masters/**/page.tsx to include juteProduction/ and juteSQC/.
- **Verification:** `npx tsc --noEmit` — ZERO errors in all 9 new juteSQC/spinning files; only the same 3 pre-existing MRPreview.test.tsx errors remain.

## 2026-06-21 - BeamingTargetMap (Beaming Standards/Targets) Master Page — spngTargetMap CLONE
- **MuiForm API changes detected:** N/A — like the other juteProduction masters this uses the inline effective-dated grid pattern (TargetMapEditor + TargetGrid), NOT MuiForm/IndexWrapper. Confirms the prior entries' divergence note.
- **Reuse decision (the task's DECIDE & REPORT):** TargetGrid is fully agnostic — it takes `paramLabels` as a prop and reads its `params`/`rows` from the backend response, so it could be reused as-is. BUT **TargetMapEditor HARDCODES** `apiRoutesPortalMasters.SPNG_TARGET_MAP_GRID` and `SPNG_TARGET_MAP_BULK_SAVE` internally (routes are NOT props; only `paramLabels` is a prop). Per the instruction's branch, I therefore **COPIED both components** into `beamingTargetMap/_components/` and swapped the two route consts to `BEAMING_TARGET_MAP_GRID`/`BEAMING_TARGET_MAP_BULK_SAVE`. Copied TargetGrid too (not just the editor) to keep the new page self-contained under its own dir (matches the learnings-log "self-contained, don't reach into other modules' dirs" principle) and to narrow its types.
- **Type narrowing in the copy:** beaming is machine-only, so the copied TargetGrid declares `IdType = "mcid"` (dropped `"qid"`) and `ValueRole = "standard" | "target"` (dropped `"actual"`). `ID_TYPE_LABELS`/`VALUE_ROLE_LABELS` narrowed to match — this is what keeps the Type dropdown single-option and the Role dropdown two-option without runtime guards.
- **[PATTERN-CHANGE]** `BEAMING_TARGET_MAP_*` (and `BM_QUALITY_*`, `BEAMING_ENTRY_*`/`BEAMING_PLANNING_GRID*`) consts ALREADY EXIST in `api.ts` `apiRoutesPortalMasters` (lines ~852-874) — the SPEC author pre-seeded them. Future beaming FE work should NOT re-add api.ts consts; grep first. The backend routers (`/api/beamingTargetMap/*`) are still SPEC-only/unimplemented (SPEC §B.5), so the page will 404 until the BE lands — FE is correct against the documented contract.
- **paramLabels:** single union map `{laid_length, cuts_per_beam, speed, eff}` passed as the editor default; the grid renders only the params the backend returns per role (standard=all four, target=speed+eff), so no per-role branching is needed in the FE — the backend's `grid_params_for` drives column visibility. This is cleaner than hardcoding two label maps.
- **Header "Type" dropdown:** kept the selector (faithful clone of spngTargetMap shape) but with one option and defaulted `idType="mcid"` so it's effectively fixed; removed the empty `<MenuItem value="">Select…</MenuItem>` for Type since there's nothing to deselect to. Role keeps its empty placeholder (gates grid load).
- **todayISO import:** kept `../../spinning/utils/spinningCalc` (verbatim from the cloned page) even though `beaming/utils/beamingCalc.ts` also exports an identical `todayISO`. Faithful-clone choice; both are valid existing siblings. Minor: a stricter "stay in your module subtree" reading would prefer the beaming one.
- **What worked well:** Reading BOTH components before deciding — the prop surface (paramLabels prop = yes, route consts = no) made the COPY-vs-reuse call unambiguous. The Fact-Forcing gate fired on every Write; pre-stating caller/Glob/data-shape/instruction each time was the unlock.
- **What should change:** Spec's Architecture Decision table still has no row for the "effective-dated inline-grid bulk-upsert master" (TargetMapEditor+TargetGrid). Add it, and note the reuse gotcha: the Editor hardcodes routes, the Grid is agnostic — clones must copy the Editor and swap 2 consts.
- **Verification:** `npx tsc --noEmit` — ZERO errors in all 3 new beamingTargetMap files; only the same 3 pre-existing MRPreview.test.tsx errors remain.

## 2026-06-21 - BeamingQuality Master Page
- **MuiForm API changes detected:** no — page deliberately uses the plain MUI TextField/Dialog list+dialog shape (bins/trollyMaster clone), not MuiForm. Simplest pattern fits a 6-field master.
- **Pattern drift from spec:** none. Matched trollyMaster exactly (mounted-guard, useSelectedCompanyCoId + useSidebarContext, fetchWithCookie, DataGrid autoHeight, sm dialog, Save-disabled guard).
- **Dependent dropdown issues:** none — jute-yarn picker auto-fills std_count from jute_yarn_count via a local handler (setForm functional update); kept std_count editable so the snapshot survives later yarn edits and so edit-mode (which has no yarn_item_id back-reference) still shows the stored count.
- **What worked well:** Item select disabled on edit to keep the duplicate key (co_id,item_id,bm_quality_code) stable; backend 400 surfaced verbatim via the {error} from fetchWithCookie into the Alert. Client-side validation (ends Number.isInteger>0, std_count>0) mirrors §A.1 before hitting the API.
- **What should change:** consts BM_QUALITY_EDIT/DELETE are base paths (caller appends /${id}?co_id=) — already documented inline in api.ts; keep that convention noted for the sibling beamingTargetMap page.
- **Verification:** `npx tsc --noEmit` — zero errors attributable to beamingQualityMaster/page.tsx.

## 2026-06-22 - BeamingQuality Master — Composite Qualities extension (Q3)
- **MuiForm API changes detected:** no — extended the same plain TextField/Dialog page in place; no MuiForm.
- **Pattern drift from spec:** none. Kept the single-file convention. Added a Switch "Is Composite" that toggles between the original simple fields and an inline COMPONENTS editor (no separate _components/ file — the editor is small and lives in the dialog, matching the "self-contained single-file master" convention for juteProduction masters).
- **Conditional-body approach:** built `detailBody` (a `Record<string, unknown>`) in handleSave that is EITHER `{is_composite:0, ends, yarn_item_id, std_count}` OR `{is_composite:1, ends:null, std_count:null, yarn_item_id:null, components:[...]}` and spread it into the create/edit body. This kept ONE save path (shared item/code/name validation + branch resolution) instead of forking the whole function — minimizes simple-path regression risk.
- **Edit detail fetch:** openEdit became async. Opens the dialog immediately seeded from the list row (responsive), THEN for `is_composite===1` rows fetches BM_QUALITY_DETAIL/{id}?co_id= and replaces components state. DataGrid edit IconButton onClick wrapped in `void openEdit(row)` since it now returns a promise (matches the existing `void handleDelete` idiom in this file).
- **Dependent dropdown issues:** the per-component yarn picker reuses the simple-path auto-fill (pick yarn -> count = jute_yarn_count, still editable) but as a per-index functional update `setComponents(prev => prev.map(...))`. component_no is auto 1..n and RE-numbered on remove so it stays contiguous; min 2 enforced both by disabling the last two delete buttons and by handleSave validation.
- **List column:** added a "Type" column rendering a Chip (Composite/Simple) off `is_composite`; `ends`/`std_count` valueFormatters now tolerate null (composite std_count is null; ends comes pre-summed from backend so no FE grid summation — only the editor shows a live sum preview).
- **What worked well:** Spreading a discriminated `detailBody` object rather than duplicating the POST/PUT calls. The saveDisabled guard mirrors handleSave's two branches exactly (simpleValid vs componentsValid) so button state and submit validation can't diverge.
- **What should change:** Spec lacks an "inline nested-rows editor inside a dialog" note — it sits between "simple MuiForm dialog" and "complex custom dialog + _components nested table". For a small N-row editor, an inline grid of TextFields in the SAME dialog (no separate component file) is the lighter, correct choice.
- **Verification:** `npx tsc --noEmit` — only the 3 pre-existing MRPreview.test.tsx errors remain; zero errors in beamingQualityMaster/page.tsx.

## 2026-06-22 - Beaming SQC (juteSQC/beaming) — single-tab Actual-RPM page
- **MuiForm API changes detected:** no — reused the existing TargetMapEditor (effective-dated inline-grid bulk-upsert pattern), no MuiForm/IndexWrapper. Confirms the running divergence note for juteProduction/juteSQC areas.
- **Reuse decision:** ZERO new components/hooks. The beaming TargetMapEditor already (a) accepts `paramLabels` as a prop and (b) its `ValueRole` union already includes `"actual"` (TargetGrid.tsx line 26) — so the SQC "Actual RPM" tab is just the editor with `valueRole="actual" paramLabels={{ speed: "RPM" }}`. No copy needed; imported across the route boundary exactly like spinning SQC imports spngTargetMap's editor. The SPEC author had pre-wired actual into the beaming components for precisely this.
- **Pattern drift from spec:** none vs the local convention. Mirrored spinning SQC page.tsx (mounted-guard + branch-resolution block + Tabs shell + per-tab date picker). Trimmed to one tab. Branch block copied verbatim (sidebarBranchIds: 1 auto / >1 select / 0 warning Alert).
- **Cross-module import path:** from juteSQC/beaming/ the editor is `../../juteProduction/masters/beamingTargetMap/_components/TargetMapEditor`; todayISO reused from `@/app/dashboardportal/juteProduction/spinning/utils/spinningCalc` (same source the spinning SQC page uses — avoids a second todayISO copy).
- **Dependent dropdown issues:** none — id_type fixed 'mcid', single role 'actual', single param 'speed'. No selectors needed beyond the date + branch.
- **act_speed/act_eff explainer:** put it in the page subtitle (helper text) per the task — states act_speed = RPM × dia × π/36 and that planning-grid act_speed/act_eff stay 0 until an actual RPM is saved here.
- **What worked well:** reading TargetMapEditor + TargetGrid BEFORE writing confirmed `paramLabels` is a prop and `actual` is already in the union → no clone, pure reuse. The Fact-Forcing gate fired once on the Write; pre-stating caller (Next.js router)/Glob(empty)/data-shape(cells speed)/instruction unlocked it.
- **What should change:** Spec Architecture Decision table still lacks the "effective-dated inline-grid bulk-upsert" row; also note that SQC "actual" pages are a thin reuse of the matching Standards/Target editor (same endpoints, role=actual) — not a new build.
- **Verification:** `npx tsc --noEmit` — zero errors in juteSQC/beaming/page.tsx; only the same 3 pre-existing MRPreview.test.tsx errors remain.
